  "solution": {
    "approach": "Compute Least Common Multiple (LCM) using relationship LCM(a, b) = (a * b) / GCD(a, b).",
    "timeComplexity": "O(log(min(a, b)))",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nlong long gcd(long long a, long long b) {\n    return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long a, b;\n    if (scanf(\"%lld %lld\", &a, &b) == 2) {\n        printf(\"%lld\\n\", (a / gcd(a, b)) * b);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <numeric>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long a, b;\n    if (cin >> a >> b) {\n        cout << (a / std::gcd(a, b)) * b << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long gcd(long a, long b) { return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b); }\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextLong()) {\n            long a = sc.nextLong(), b = sc.nextLong();\n            System.out.println((a / gcd(a, b)) * b);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys, math\n\ndef main():\n    parts = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        a, b = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])\n        print((a * b) // math.gcd(a, b))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\nfunction gcd(a, b) { return b === 0n ? a : gcd(b, a % b); }\nfunction main() {\n    const parts = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (parts.length >= 2) {\n        const a = BigInt(parts[0]), b = BigInt(parts[1]);\n        console.log(((a / gcd(a, b)) * b).toString());\n    }\n}\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Use Euclidean algorithm to find GCD, then calculate LCM = (a / GCD(a, b)) * b."
  },
